Frequently asked questions about our library
--------------------------------------------
Q: Are there two different libraries for C and C++?
A: Yes, but if you start using our C library, and then transfer to C++,
   the conversion is very simple.

Q: On what platforms does it run?
A: It runs on most UNIX workstations (SUN, HP, MIPS, SONY, ...), on IBM PC
   (DOS or MS Windows), and on Macintosh (PWB). The library is not hardware
   or OS dependent. We have users on a variety of computers, including
   VMS VAX and Amdahl.

Q: With what compilers does it run?
A: The library is shipped with script files that allow you to recompile the
   library with different compilers. Even if the script file is not included
   for some particular compiler, it is usually easy to create your own script
   file.  Examples of the compilers:   AT&T, SUN, HP, DEC-ULTRIX, AIX RS6000,
   BORLAND, ZORTECH, MICROSOFT, GNU.

Q: How much does it cost?
A: See file A:\BUSINESS\PRICES
    
Q: What sort of documentation will I recieve?
A: You will recieve two Users Guides, each over 250 pp.(one for C, one for C++).
   Also, the library includes an automatic documentation generator, which
   allows you to print the Reference Guide (over 350 pp.) yourself.
   This information is retrieved directly from the library source, and is
   therefore guaranteed to always be up to date.
   In addition to this printed information, the library has an intelligent
   on-line querry system.
      
Q: What kind of library is it (user interface or collection classes)?
A: This is a new style of library, which has advantages of both systems.
   All classes are custom generated, flat, and very efficient. There is 
   no common class from which other objects must be derived.
   For more details, see directories BROCHURE and TUTORIAL.

Q: What classes does it contain?
A: Look at file CLASSES.

Q: Are there any restrictions in using the library?
A: Practically none. You can even ship the source of the library with
   your product. The only restriction is that you must not distribute
   our code generator (users of your software do not need the code 
   generator to recompile your product). For the full text of the legal
   licence, look at A:\BUSINESS\LICENSE and A:\BUSINESS\PRICES
   There are no royalties for using the library.

Q: What about support?
A: The library has been in heavy use on large commercial applications
   for over 3 years, and it is very solid. If you find any bug, we 
   fix it immediately. Additions, improvements, introductory
   courses, and help with custom design is available on a contract basis.

Q: How to order the library?
A: The order form is in file A:\BUSINESS\ORDER
